  "final_output": "The scheduled nightly supplier price import caused the Catalog replica lag. The cron job started at 00:30 UTC. Catalog committed 10 batches, and the job finished at 00:35:48 UTC after it updated 48,210 rows.\n\nThe replica took longer to apply the batch writes. Lag peaked at 44 seconds at 00:36 UTC. ReplicaLagHigh resolved at 00:41 UTC. Lag returned to normal by 00:44 UTC.\n\nProduct pages could briefly show old prices. Checkout reads from the primary database, so customers paid the correct price. Checkout success was 99.05% during the import window and 97.42% before it. No orders were stuck during either window.\n\nNo immediate action is needed. If the alert fires every night, review the batch size with the Catalog team.",
